{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bee-logical/AIDLC/main/docs/aidlc.config.schema.json",
  "$comment": "POLYREPO EXAMPLE. Copy the workspace+repos shape into your aidlc.config.json when the workspace holds several git repos. In poly mode the top-level git/stack/ux blocks are ignored — each repo carries its own. This file lives at the WORKSPACE ROOT (the control plane); the product repos are subfolders under workspace.root.",
  "project": {
    "key": "PROJ",
    "name": "Example polyrepo product"
  },
  "workItems": {
    "source": "markdown",
    "jira": { "site": "", "project": "", "statusMap": {} },
    "ado": { "org": "", "project": "", "statusMap": {} }
  },
  "workspace": {
    "layout": "poly",
    "root": "."
  },
  "repos": [
    {
      "name": "backend",
      "path": "backend",
      "role": "REST API service — NestJS + Postgres",
      "host": "github",
      "remote": "origin",
      "defaultBranch": "main",
      "branchPattern": "{type}/{id}-{slug}",
      "stack": { "frontend": null, "backend": "nestjs", "databases": ["postgres"] },
      "labels": ["backend", "api", "server"],
      "default": true,
      "$comment2": "saas = the runtime constraints that change how code must be WRITTEN, derived by /aidlc:adopt from static evidence. OMIT any field the scan could not evidence — an absent field means the agent briefs stay silent, and a guessed `tenancy` misdirects every review from here on. It informs the implementer/reviewer/security briefs; the only things it GATES are a destructive migration under liveDataConstraint=expand-contract (review blocker) and a diff touching apiContracts/authPaths/tenantIsolationPaths (reviewed regardless of cadence).",
      "saas": {
        "tenancy": "shared-schema",
        "tenantKey": "tenant_id",
        "tenantIsolationPaths": ["src/common/tenant.middleware.ts", "prisma/rls/"],
        "authPaths": ["src/auth/"],
        "billingPaths": ["src/billing/"],
        "featureFlags": { "provider": "LaunchDarkly", "paths": ["src/flags/"], "required": true },
        "migrations": { "tool": "Prisma", "directory": "prisma/migrations" },
        "liveDataConstraint": "expand-contract",
        "apiContracts": [{ "kind": "openapi", "path": "openapi/public-v1.yaml", "public": true }],
        "environments": [{ "name": "staging", "kind": "staging" }, { "name": "production", "kind": "production" }],
        "deployStrategy": "canary",
        "freezeWindows": [{ "when": "Fri 16:00 -> Mon 09:00 UTC", "source": ".github/workflows/deploy.yml:8 schedule guard" }],
        "compliance": [{ "regime": "soc2", "signal": "docs/security/soc2-controls.md lists CC6 evidence owners" }],
        "messaging": [{ "name": "BullMQ", "kind": "queue", "paths": ["src/jobs/"] }],
        "observability": [{ "name": "Sentry", "paths": ["src/main.ts"] }],
        "source": "codebase-scan"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "platform",
      "path": "platform",
      "role": "Shared platform monorepo — pnpm workspaces + Turborepo",
      "host": "github",
      "remote": "origin",
      "defaultBranch": "main",
      "branchPattern": "{type}/{id}-{slug}",
      "stack": { "frontend": null, "backend": null, "databases": [] },
      "labels": ["platform", "shared"],
      "$comment2": "MONOREPO EXAMPLE — one git repo, many independently-owned packages. It stays a single repos[] entry on purpose: repos[] is the GIT boundary (this repo has one) and packages[] is the OWNERSHIP boundary inside it. That is also what makes this hybrid workspace — a monorepo beside single-app repos — representable with no new layout value. An item routes to a package (explicit -> label -> path -> default -> grounding -> ask); its gate, stack, ux and PR label scope to it, but it is still ONE branch and ONE PR. `releasable` is only true where the tooling can actually cut a per-package release (here: changesets); `dependsOn` sequences cross-package work so a shared package lands before its consumers.",
      "packages": [
        {
          "name": "@acme/shared",
          "path": "packages/shared",
          "role": "Shared TypeScript types and generated API client",
          "labels": ["shared", "types"],
          "stack": { "frontend": null, "backend": "typescript-library", "databases": [] },
          "releasable": true
        },
        {
          "name": "@acme/admin",
          "path": "packages/admin",
          "role": "Internal admin console — Next.js",
          "labels": ["admin", "console", "frontend"],
          "stack": { "frontend": "nextjs", "backend": null, "databases": [] },
          "dependsOn": ["@acme/shared"],
          "ux": {
            "enabled": true,
            "target": "desktop-web",
            "renderBaseUrl": "http://localhost:3002",
            "uiPaths": ["packages/admin/app/**", "packages/admin/components/**"]
          },
          "default": true
        },
        {
          "name": "acme-worker",
          "path": "packages/worker",
          "role": "Async job worker — Python + Celery",
          "labels": ["worker", "python", "jobs"],
          "stack": { "frontend": null, "backend": "python-celery", "databases": ["postgres"] },
          "dependsOn": ["@acme/shared"]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "frontend",
      "path": "frontend",
      "role": "Customer web app — Next.js",
      "host": "github",
      "remote": "origin",
      "defaultBranch": "main",
      "branchPattern": "{type}/{id}-{slug}",
      "stack": { "frontend": "nextjs", "backend": null, "databases": [] },
      "labels": ["frontend", "web", "ui"],
      "ux": {
        "enabled": true,
        "target": "desktop-web",
        "renderBaseUrl": "http://localhost:3000",
        "uiPaths": ["app/**", "src/app/**", "components/**", "src/components/**", "**/*.tsx", "**/*.css"],
        "figma": {
          "enabled": true,
          "url": "https://www.figma.com/design/AbC123dEf456/Acme-Web",
          "fileKey": "AbC123dEf456",
          "screens": { "/": "1-2", "/dashboard": "12-408", "/settings": "12-509" },
          "jury": "suggest",
          "maxFidelityRounds": 2
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "website",
      "path": "website",
      "role": "Marketing site — Next.js static",
      "host": "azure-repos",
      "remote": "origin",
      "defaultBranch": "main",
      "branchPattern": "{type}/{id}-{slug}",
      "$comment": "GitFlow example: feature work branches from and integrates into `develop`, never `main`. mergeStrategy/commitStyle/conventionsSource are the project's OWN conventions — `default` would mean AIDLC's defaults are in use and were not detected.",
      "integrationBranch": "develop",
      "longLivedBranches": ["main", "develop", "release/*"],
      "commitStyle": "conventional",
      "mergeStrategy": "squash",
      "conventionsSource": "codebase-scan",
      "stack": { "frontend": "nextjs", "backend": null, "databases": [] },
      "labels": ["website", "marketing", "landing"],
      "ux": {
        "enabled": true,
        "target": "desktop-web",
        "renderBaseUrl": "http://localhost:3001",
        "uiPaths": ["app/**", "src/**", "**/*.tsx", "**/*.css"]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "mobile",
      "path": "mobile",
      "role": "React Native / Expo app",
      "host": "github",
      "remote": "origin",
      "defaultBranch": "main",
      "branchPattern": "{type}/{id}-{slug}",
      "stack": { "frontend": "react-native", "backend": null, "databases": [] },
      "labels": ["mobile", "app", "ios", "android"]
    }
  ],
  "pipeline": {
    "autonomy": "high",
    "maxFixCycles": 3,
    "architectThreshold": "M",
    "securityReviewPaths": ["**/auth/**", "**/*.env*", "package.json", "**/middleware*"],
    "envFileAccess": "deny",
    "gates": {
      "ambiguousRequirements": "assume-and-log",
      "$comment": "verify = the project's REAL gate, executed IN ORDER by the run skill. Populated by /aidlc:adopt-apply from a scan, or written by hand. Resolution LAYERS narrowest -> broadest (repos.<repo>.packages.<pkg>.steps, then packages.<pkg>.steps, then repos.<repo>.steps, then the top-level steps); each layer contributes its own order but only for gate names no narrower layer claimed — so a package declaring its own `test` still INHERITS the repo's `lint`. Do not read it as replace: a gate that vanished is indistinguishable from one that passed. Use `node <plugin>/skills/run/resolve-gate.mjs` rather than re-deriving it. Note the `absent` entries — a gate the project does NOT have is kept on purpose so every run reports it as a coverage hole instead of counting it green; that is also how a package deliberately opts OUT of a repo-level gate.",
      "verify": {
        "maxItemMinutes": 10,
        "steps": [
          { "name": "lint", "status": "present", "cmd": "npm run lint", "required": true, "scope": "repo" },
          { "name": "typecheck", "status": "present", "cmd": "npm run typecheck", "required": true, "scope": "repo" },
          { "name": "test", "status": "present", "cmd": "npm test", "required": true, "scope": "repo" }
        ],
        "repos": {
          "backend": {
            "steps": [
              { "name": "lint", "status": "present", "cmd": "npm run lint", "required": true, "scope": "repo", "providedByHook": "husky" },
              { "name": "typecheck", "status": "present", "cmd": "npm run typecheck", "required": true, "scope": "repo" },
              { "name": "test", "status": "present", "cmd": "npm test", "required": true, "scope": "repo", "timeoutMinutes": 20, "environmentDependent": true, "services": ["postgres"] },
              { "name": "format", "status": "absent", "required": false, "scope": "repo" }
            ]
          },
          "mobile": {
            "steps": [
              { "name": "lint", "status": "present", "cmd": "npm run lint", "required": true, "scope": "repo" },
              { "name": "test", "status": "absent", "required": false, "scope": "repo" }
            ]
          },
          "platform": {
            "$comment": "Monorepo with an affected-graph runner: the repo gate runs AFFECTED targets only, and the run report must name the affected set. The per-package blocks below then LAYER over it — acme-worker's pytest replaces the repo's `test` while still inheriting the repo's `lint` and `typecheck`, and @acme/admin declares `typecheck` absent to opt OUT explicitly (which keeps it visible as a coverage hole rather than erasing it).",
            "steps": [
              { "name": "lint", "status": "present", "cmd": "pnpm turbo run lint --filter=...[origin/main]", "required": true, "scope": "affected" },
              { "name": "typecheck", "status": "present", "cmd": "pnpm turbo run typecheck --filter=...[origin/main]", "required": true, "scope": "affected" },
              { "name": "test", "status": "present", "cmd": "pnpm turbo run test --filter=...[origin/main]", "required": true, "scope": "affected" }
            ],
            "packages": {
              "acme-worker": {
                "steps": [
                  { "name": "test", "status": "present", "cmd": "uv run pytest", "cwd": "packages/worker", "required": true, "scope": "package", "environmentDependent": true, "services": ["postgres"] }
                ]
              },
              "@acme/admin": {
                "steps": [
                  { "name": "typecheck", "status": "absent", "required": false, "scope": "package" }
                ]
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "verification": {
      "mode": "auto",
      "reviewer": "on-demand",
      "qa": "on-demand",
      "security": "per-epic",
      "securityConfirm": true
    }
  },
  "marketplace": {
    "repo": "bee-logical/AIDLC",
    "promotionBranchPrefix": "promote/"
  }
}
